  "solution": "Logic: (1st number × 5) +5 = 2nd number\n\nGiven:\n\n__\n \n• 12 : 65\n\n**(12 × 5)**__ + 5 = 65\n\n__**60 **____**+ 5**__ = 65 \n\n65 = 65 (LHS = RHS)\n\n__\n \n• 13 : 70\n\n(13 × 5)__ + 5 = 70\n\n__65 ____+ 5__ = 70 \n\n70 = 70 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo, \n\n__\n \n• Option - (1): 14 : 65\n\n(14 × 5)__ + 5 = 65\n\n__70 ____+ 5__ = 65 \n\n75 ≠ 65 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n__\n \n• Option - (2) : 15 : 80\n\n(15 × 5)__ + 5 = 80\n\n__75 ____+ 5__ = 80 \n\n**80 = 80 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n__\n \n• Option - (3): 16 : 75\n\n(16 × 5)__ + 5 = 75\n\n__80 ____+ 5__ =75 \n\n85 ≠ 75 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n__\n \n• Option - (4): 18 : 85\n\n(18 × 5)__ + 5 = 85\n\n__90 ____+ 5__ = 85 \n\n95 ≠ 85 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nHence, \"Option - (2)\" is the correct answer.",
